WEBVTT

00:01.760 --> 00:05.360
Building a schedule for one month takes hours.

00:05.680 --> 00:08.240
You have to think about everything: days off,

00:08.400 --> 00:10.560
holidays, who can do which shift,

00:10.880 --> 00:13.200
how many people each section needs.

00:13.300 --> 00:16.200
With ShiftSmith, you just click "Generate".

00:16.200 --> 00:18.120
So, let me show you with a blank schedule,

00:18.280 --> 00:20.680
for example, January 2027.

00:21.000 --> 00:23.960
Click "Generate", then "Generate draft".

00:25.480 --> 00:28.280
So, behind this button, there is a solver.

00:28.520 --> 00:30.680
It knows all the rules of the hotel:

00:31.000 --> 00:33.120
contracts, rest days,

00:33.360 --> 00:35.440
the shifts each person can do,

00:35.760 --> 00:38.160
and the staff each section needs.

00:40.630 --> 00:43.430
A few seconds later, you have a full schedule:

00:43.950 --> 00:46.190
every section, every employee,

00:46.510 --> 00:48.400
every day.

00:48.500 --> 00:53.870
So this schedule is now generated as a draft,

00:54.110 --> 00:56.750
so no employee can see it for now.

00:57.390 --> 01:02.070
If you're happy with the schedule, you just click

01:02.070 --> 01:07.900
on "Publish", and the employees will now see the schedule.

01:07.900 --> 01:12.800
So what took a whole afternoon now takes a coffee break.
